WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.602
[music playing]

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:08.141
- Man, those percebes
were absolutely amazing.

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:09.609
But super simple.

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:12.512
Now according to Kiko,
they're not as simple to get.

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:15.615
He's arranged for me to
meet a very talented local

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:19.085
see barnacle harvester
who'll show me how to really

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.620
get these prized assets.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:28.261
- Ricardo.

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:29.629
- Hey Gordon.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:30.930
- Hi bud.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.632
- It's amazing today.

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:33.733
- Good to see you, bud.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.001
I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:37.637
- Ricardo Kazmi is a
percebes harvester.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.939
That does not look easy.

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.541
- We'll see.

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.843
- He forages year-round for the
barnacles, and knows the waters

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.912
here like the back of his hand.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.147
Look at those waves.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.748
- Going to be rough.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:52.452
The harder the waves are, and
the deeper the percebes are--

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:53.520
- Right.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.188
- --the bigger they
are and the better.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:56.089
- Per-seh-bi.

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:56.856
- We good.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:57.757
Per-seh-bish.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:58.758
- Per-seh-bish.

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.493
- Yeah, almost, almost.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.761
- Let's go.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:02.695
Wetsuit on?

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:03.696
- Yeah.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.039
- Is size important for you?

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:13.940
Or thickness?

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.108
No--

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:16.142
- We're talking
about the percebes?

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.310
- We are talking about percebes.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:18.311
- Of course it is.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:19.646
- The thickness or the size?

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.046
- Both.

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.448
- Both.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:22.982
- 2 centimeters, and like
thickness of a finger.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.017
- Gotcha.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:25.084
- Those are the ones perfect.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:26.419
- Gotcha.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:29.889
- They will cost roughly
90, 100 euros kilograms.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:30.890
- 100 euros a kilo?

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.225
- Yeah.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:33.660
Because you're risking
your life doing this.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:36.763
- Yeah [muted] I have to
check on my insurance.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:46.706
Percebes are even harder to
gather than to pronounce.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:50.643
Each year in Portugal, a handful
of people die collecting them.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:55.114
Hopefully the ocean is
hungry for a new victim.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.450
- We need to be
constantly watching.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.619
Never turn your
back to the ocean.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:00.420
Never.

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:01.187
- Never turn your back, no.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.856
Got you, captain.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.024
Man, you're like Spider Man.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.993
Seriously, can you slow down?

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.029
Now all of a sudden you start
to see the size of those waves.

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.764
- You don't see them yet.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.566
You will feel them.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.567
Time to get wet.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.672
- [muted] Really?

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:28.147
For a veteran like Ricardo,
this is a walk in the park.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:31.718
But it makes me wish
I had a stunt double.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.386
- Ready yourself.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.625
- [muted]

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:39.425
- How was it?

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.361
We need to move from there.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:44.097
- You can hide in
the [muted] hole.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:46.099
- OK, Chief, now
it's the timing.

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:48.101
- Finding the right
size barnacles

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.403
takes incredible
timing, great strength,

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.672
and just a touch of crazy.

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:57.977
This is not like
foraging berries.

00:02:58.044 --> 00:03:00.313
This is foraging on steroids.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.082
[muted] now that is amazing.

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:04.217
Bloody hell.

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:06.553
Aren't they beautiful?

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:07.887
Really beautiful.

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:08.788
Wow.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.323
- Now it's your turn.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.225
But first we need to wait,
there is coming a massive set.

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.226
- Is there really?

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:15.094
- Look at the lines, let's--

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:22.535
- [muted] [muted] This is mad.

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:23.636
That is strong.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.111
- Be careful.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.584
- We need to move.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.551
Stand.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:42.455
- [muted]

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:43.890
- Gordon, hide, hide,
hide, hide, hide.

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:46.659
There is a big set coming.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.661
[waves crashing]

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:55.735
- [muted] I can't get it.

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.070
- Let's search another hole.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.072
- With the final cook
in a few days time,

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:01.708
failure is not an option.

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:06.179
So Ricardo suggest we try
our luck in a different spot.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:08.615
- Try to catch those
ones, come on Gordon.

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:12.852
Got them?

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:14.354
Careful.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.955
- You start to realize the
danger when you're chipping

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:17.390
away, the waves coming in.

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.959
You let go, do you
let go of the goods

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:23.763
do you save onto your life?

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:33.873
[waves crashing]

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.675
- Nice size.

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:39.912
- You did it.

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.581
- 100 euros a kilo.

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:43.149
One of the most
expensive shellfish

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.584
anywhere on the planet.

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:46.786
I see why now, because
they're the most dangerous.

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:47.487
- Let's go.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:48.821
- Amazing.

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:52.191
This confirms how rugged,
but stunning this country is,

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.359
especially on the coastline.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:55.028
Because look at it.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:58.564
To the naked eye just looks
like waves pounding the rocks.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.767
But there's so much
activity under there,

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:01.934
and it's incredible.

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:02.835
Good job, bud.

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:05.705
Honestly.

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:07.040
Amazing.

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:10.810
Adventurous, dangerous,
stupid and delicious.

